---
title: Connection Sequence
---
sequenceDiagram
    participant UI
    participant Root
    participant Worker
    participant PIX as PIX pool (edgli)
    participant Exit as Exit node
    participant Server as gvpn server (at exit)
    participant Relayer as Curvy relayer (via exit)

    UI->>Root: Connect
    Root->>Worker: Connect
    Root->>UI: Ack

    rect rgba(128, 128, 128, 0.1)
    Note over Worker,Server: Probe session (TCP, long-lived, one per probed exit)
    Worker->>Server: open bridge session
    Worker->>Server: version, ping, load checks
    Note over Worker: probe ready: the connect starts
    end

    par side-car (step 0)
        Worker->>Relayer: open relayer side-car (TCP, no PIX, fixed local port)
        Worker->>PIX: release held deposits
    and steps 1-5
        Worker->>Root: KillswitchLockdown (tunnel closed)
        Note over Worker: WG keys (kept from the last attempt)
        Worker->>Server: register WG pubkey (over the probe session)
    end

    Worker->>Exit: open WG session (UDP, UsePIX), spliced into the NepTUN pump
    Exit-->>PIX: deposit request (SURB)
    PIX->>Relayer: fee, allocate, proof, submit (over the side-car)
    Worker->>Root: SetupTunnel
    Root->>Worker: TunnelReady (TUN fd via SCM_RIGHTS)
    Worker->>Root: KillswitchLockdown (gateway only)

    loop until the exit serves: AwaitingPayment while its keep-alives arrive
        Worker->>Exit: ping 10.128.0.1 through the tunnel
    end
    Note over Exit: deposit seen on chain: the session is served

    Worker->>Root: KillswitchLockdown (tunnel open)
    Worker->>Root: Connected
    Note over Exit,Relayer: later chunks: deposit request on the WG session, payment over the side-car
